```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Tuesday, June 18, 2024, in Committee
Room 104 and via electronic mceting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Scott Roybal, Chairman. Pete Layboum. Dr. Rinne, and Tom
Segrave.
AGENDA ITEMS
11.
ORDINANCE —3” READING
— Amending Sections 1.4.3 Defined Terms and 2.2.6
Temporary Use Approval of the Unified Development Code, adding a minimum of
fourteen days.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 3Td and final reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report.
t2.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
-- Amending Section
I .4.4.c Service Uses, Table 5-1
Zoning District Uses, Section 5.7.4 Child Care Uses, and Table 6-2 Required Parking of
the Unified Development Code, changing Child Care Requirements.
Mr. Laybourn declared a conflict and excused himself from the meeting for discussion and vote
on item #12.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion failed with
Dr. Rinne voting “NO” and Mr. Segrave voting “YES”.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and committee
member Rinne commented on the item.
13,
ORDINANCE _3m READING
— Creating Section 10.24.190. Critical Traffic Control
Areas; Creation and Administration; Enhanced Penalties, of the Municipal Code of the City
of Cheyenne, Wyoming. authorizing the designation of Critical Traffic Control Areas and
authorizing enhanced penalties as specified.
Mr. Layboum moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Mayor Patrick Collins advised the committee that no changes have been made since the ordinance
was approved on
2nd1 reading and was available for questions.
Committee member Layboum
commented on the item.
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
14.
ORDINANCE —2 READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne changing the zoning classification from MUB Mixed-Use Business to CB
Community Business for land located northeast of the intersection of Cheyenne Street and
Ridge Road. (SPONSOR
— MR. ROYBAL)
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on
2nd reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and committee
member Rinne commented on the item.
17.
RESOLUTION
Approving the Jolly Rogers Urban Renewal Plan and the Jolly Rogers
Urban Renewal Project pursuant to Wyoming Statute Section 15-9-110.
(SPONSOR
-
MR. ROYBAL)
Mr. Segrave moved to adopt, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried with Dr. Rinne and Mr.
Segrave voting “YES” and Mr. Layboum voting “NO”.
Charles Bloom, Planning & Development Department Director, provided a staff report and Mark
Christensen, AVI P.C., provided additional information. Additional comment was made by Tom
Cobb, City Engineer.
18.
RESOLUTION
— Authorizing the Mayor to execute all necessary documents related to the
transfer of a specified portion of the property located at 2014 Dell Range Boulevard.
(SPONSOR - MR. ROYBAL)
Mr. Laybourn moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Segrave.
Motion carried by unanimous voice
vote.
Chief John Kopper, Fire & Rescue, provided a staff report and committee member Segrave
commented on the item.
19.
RESOLUTION
— Expressing the appreciation of the Governing Body for the work of
Director Nemecek. Director Sanchez. and their respective departments, on correcting
deficiencies and improving and maintaining certain exterior components of the Municipal
Building. (SPONSOR—MR. SEGRAVE)
Mr. Segrave moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Laybourn.
Motion carried by unanimous voice
vote.
Tom Segrave. Ward III City Councilman and member of the Public Services Committee provided
an explanation for the proposed resolution.
Vicki Nemecek. Public Works Director, provided a
brief review of exterior upgrades to the Municipal building.
Committee member Layhourn
commented on the item.
```

